      "summary": "Monday 05/10 We are Open today with another Bluebird day to kick off your week! We have the classic spring snow conditions at the moment with a firm snowpack in places to start, otherwise becoming soft and springy throughout the day. The forecast is for another fine day and light winds - you can't get much better mountain weather than this! From today we have switched to our Spring Opening Hours - 9am - 4:30pm. Main Basin and Valley will be open from 9am, with Captains, T-Bar and Soho to follow. We have the ANC Halfpipe competition on today you can view from behind the ropeline on the decks of the pipe. There will be some great viewing to see our local athletes and international athletes compete! The Pipe will be closed for the Event. Friendly reminder, we have also switched to our spring Pines Shuttle and bus schedule! Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 10 / 10 Runs Open - / 38 Percent open 90 %",
